   "html_text": "Definition 1.1 (Game in Strategic Form) A game in strategic form is a tuple ⟦M⟧ where ⟦M⟧ is a nonempty finite set of players, for each ⟦M⟧ , ⟦M⟧ is a nonempty set of actions for player ⟦M⟧ , and for each ⟦M⟧ , ⟦M⟧ is player ⟦M⟧ ’s utility function, where ⟦M⟧ is the set of strategy profiles.",
   "md_text": "Definition 1.1 (Game in Strategic Form) A game in strategic form is a tuple ⟦M⟧ where ⟦M⟧ is a nonempty finite set of players, for each ⟦M⟧ , ⟦M⟧ is a nonempty set of actions for player ⟦M⟧ , and for each ⟦M⟧ , ⟦M⟧ is player ⟦M⟧ ’s utility function, where ⟦M⟧ is the set of strategy profiles."
